### Bloat / size tooling (owner ask — memory only; not installed, not committed)

Deps are lean; perceived bloat is mostly **code concentration** (`explain.py` ~2591 LOC). When owner wants a pass later:

| Tool | Use |
|---|---|
| **vulture** | Dead / unused code |
| **radon** (`cc`, `mi`) | Complexity / maintainability hotspots |
| **ruff** (unused-import rules) | Quick unused imports if adopted |
| **cloc** / **tokei** | LOC heat map by file |
| **pipdeptree** / `uv tree` | Dependency tree (expect little) |

Product ROA / impact bar still decides whether a surface should exist — tools find dead/complex code, they don’t replace that judgment. Prefer a targeted `explain.py` look over a drive-by rewrite.

